{"Title":"An Act to support cannabis equity businesses","BillNumber":"S53","DocketNumber":"SD1993","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:32:59.013"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:32:59.0133333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S53/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Lewis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 53) of Jason M. Lewis for legislation to support cannabis equity businesses.  Cannabis Policy.","DocumentText":"\tSection 4 of chapter 94G of the General Laws, is hereby amended by adding the following subsection:-\r\n\t(m) The cannabis control commission, in consultation with the Massachusetts cannabis advisory board, shall create a searchable online database of all operational cannabis dispensaries that allows users to identify economic empowerment applicants, social equity program participants, disadvantaged business enterprises, unionized organizations, organizations under investigation, and other criteria identified by the commission and advisory board available on the commission's website no later than Dec. 31, 2024.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J50","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J50"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}